From fa8ab359d2704dbd4b6a20e3e41a59da93b9127a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:48:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 126/250] fix(pypto-x): make the torch linear bridge fail open
 on real build failures (W8J J1 fix 1)

V8J-D1: read-only cache directories, clang failures and artifact load
failures leaked raw PermissionError / Avx512CompileError /
CpuAvx512RuntimeError through both torch.ops.pypto_x.linear and
linear_strict, so the fail-open contract did not hold and no fallback event
was recorded.

- linear_kernel: wrap every real build/lower/compile/load exception into
  PyPTOXBuildError with cache_unwritable / compile_failed / load_failed /
  build_io_error / build_failed reason codes; PyPTOXBuildError now derives
  from PyPTOXUnsupportedError so strict callers catch one structured type;
  optional clang override for failure-injection tests.
- torch_ops: the fail-open op absorbs the real exception families as a
  second line of defence; the strict op wraps any raw leak into a
  structured PyPTOXUnsupportedError.
- V8J-D2: a content-addressed .so whose bytes no longer match its filename
  digest (or the sidecar digest) is quarantined as
  *.corrupt-<stamp>-<pid> before the rebuild; the bytes are kept for audit
  instead of making the digest path permanently unusable.
- V8J-D3: pack_weight copies the transposed payload directly into the
  handle tensor (one np.copyto instead of four payload copies).
- V8J-D4: docs/tests now state that a requires_grad forward falls back to
  F.linear but .backward() raises "no autograd formula" (J1 is
  inference-only).
- bf16 no-bias correctness is K-bucketed: bitwise for the sampled K <= 128
  shapes, one-LSB tolerance above, because the rebased packed plane can
  flip one bf16 ULP on a near-zero output (the independent verifier
  measured 6.104e-05 at K=1024).
- the packed payload-4 plane is declared by the plan while this bridge still
  executes the legacy ZMM symbol; LinearKernelEntry now records
  declared_plane/executed_plane so the divergence is explicit instead of
  silent.

New real-failure tests: read-only cache directory, fake clang compiler,
corrupt .so quarantine/rebuild with and without a sidecar, payload-3
sidecar invalidation after rebasing onto payload 4, pack copy count,
autograd behaviour, the K buckets and the declared/executed plane metadata.
